+#### Render video..., Render cover...
+
+Grayed out if not in NW.js app.
+Show a popup form, confirming which
+renders and saves the video or the cover image to local filesystem
+using [sunniesnow-record](https://www.npmjs.com/package/sunniesnow-record).
+
+When calling its API, generate the level file in the memory and provide it as a `Blob` object.
+For rendering video, always use the currently loaded music as the selected music in the rendering
+(so rendering video is grayed out if no music is loaded);
+for rendering either, always use the currently loaded image as the background provided for sunniesnow-record,
+and use `background: "none"` in the options if no image is loaded.
+Also properly set `assetsDir` so that sunniesnow-record reuses the fonts bundled by sviber
+instead of downloading them.
+
+The popup form has an input field for the output path in the local filesystem.
+Near the input field, there is a "Browse" button for using a file dialogue to pick the path.
+Then, there are input fields for customizable options
+that will be passed to sunniesnow-record.
+Note that not every option accepted by sunniesnow-record should customizable.
+
+For rendering video, the customizable options are:
+
+- `nickname`: Use the chart's `charter` property as default.
+- `avatar`.
+- `avatarOnline`, `avatarUpload`, `avatarGravatar`:
+  Depending on which value is set for `avatar`, at most one input field is enabled.
+- Whether to use bundled FFmpeg. This option does not appear if bundled FFmpeg is not available
+  (e.g., when directly running with `nw .` in the source repo or if the FFmpeg bundling was disabled when the build script ran).
+- `speed`: default 2, regardless of editor preferences.
+- `width`, `height`: default 1920 and 1080.
+- `fps`: default 60.
+- `resultsDuration`: default 1.
+- `waitForMusic`: default true.
+
+For rendering cover, the customizable options are:
+
+- `nickname`, `avatar`, `avatarOnline`, `avatarUpload`, `avatarGravatar`, `width`, `height`:
+  Handle them in the same way as those in options for rendering video.
+- `coverThemeImageX`, `coverThemeImageY`, `coverThemeImageWidth`:
+  Show a GUI widget powered by PixiJS for setting those parameters instead of having input fields.
+  The canvas has the same aspect ratio as the loaded image, and the loaded image is a controllable sprite.
+  The user can move the sprite by dragging and zoom the sprite by scrolling.
+  There is a diamond shape area indicating the resultant part of the image shown as the cover theme image,
+  outside which the sprite appears darkened.
+
+After confirming the popup form, show another popup form while waiting for the rendering.
+If rendering video, show a progress bar
+(empty when rendering the zeroth frame and full when rendering the last frame)
+and a text near it saying the current status of the rendering.
+This popup form can only be confirmed after the rendering finishes.
+When the rendering finishes, another button shows, clicking which opens the directory
+containing the rendered file using the system file explorer.
