+### Conflicting bg patterns
+
+For an event $E$, denote its time $t_0(E)$ and its end time $t_1(E)$.
+If two background patterns $E_1$ and $E_2$ satisfy
+$t_0(E_2)\le t_1(E_1)$ and $t_0(E_1)\le t_1(E_2)$, then they are conflicting background patterns.
+This check checks that there are no conflicting background patterns.
+When a violation is clicked, both background patterns are selected.
+
+There is a boolean parameter for this check,
+setting which to false makes the check less strict:
+the condition of confliction becomes $t_0(E_2)<t_1(E_1)$ and $t_0(E_1)<t_1(E_2)$.
+It is true by default.
